<title>USA: Snyder Oil says it expands buyback program.</title>
<headline>Snyder Oil says it expands buyback program.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snyder Oil Corp said Wednesday it expanded its securities repurchase program by $20 million to a total of $50 million.</p>
<p>The company said the expansion may involve the purchase of common stock, six percent preferred stock and seven convertible subordinated notes due 2001.</p>
<p>The company said it has so far acquired 1.9 million common shares and $4.6 million in subordinated notes at a total cost of approximately $30 million.</p>
</text>
